// ============================ The document shape ============================
//
// The gRPC rendering of the OpenNLP 3.0 document container: the
// analyzed text plus any number of named annotation layers, each layer a list of
// annotations whose value type is fixed by the layer. Layer ids are namespaced
// strings exactly as in the Java container ("opennlp:" prefixes every layer the
// toolkit itself produces; other producers use their own prefix), so the key
// space stays open while every annotation value stays strongly typed through
// the oneof below.
//
// Layers the v1 server emits, each only when its producing step ran:
//    opennlp:sentences   positional, string values: the covered sentence text.
//    opennlp:tokens      positional, string values: the covered token text.
//    opennlp:pos         positional, string values: the POS tag, one annotation
//                        per token, span-aligned with opennlp:tokens.
//    opennlp:lemmas      positional, string values: the lemma, span-aligned with
//                        opennlp:tokens.
//    opennlp:entities    positional, entity values: the complete NamedEntity,
//                        including provider and geocoding provenance.
//    opennlp:chunks      positional, syntactic-chunk values: each complete
//                        ChunkSpan and its provider provenance.
//    opennlp:parses      positional, tree values: every constituency parse of
//                        each parsed sentence, with the primary first.
//    opennlp:sentiment   positional, category values: per-sentence label and
//                        score, the span covering the sentence.
//    opennlp:language    document-scoped, category values: the detected language
//                        code and its confidence; with a positive
//                        AnalysisOptions.ranked_language_count, the ranked
//                        predictions best first.
//    opennlp:categories  document-scoped, category values: the whole
//                        classification distribution, best category first.
//    opennlp:embeddings  positional, embedding values: sentence vectors and, when
//                        requested, the document centroid, told apart by granularity.
//    opennlp:word-types  positional, word-type values: the closed UAX #29
//                        DocumentWordType per token, present only for uax29.
//    opennlp:stopwords   positional, string values: the covered text of each
//                        token the stopword list matched.
//    opennlp:terms:<DIMENSION>  positional, string values: the per-token
//                        normalized form of one requested term dimension,
//                        span-aligned with opennlp:tokens.
//    opennlp:subwords    positional, subword values: the SentencePiece encoding
//                        of the whole document text, each piece with its
//                        vocabulary id (from PIPELINE_STEP_SUBWORD_TOKENIZE).
//    opennlp:stems       positional, stem values: the stem and its complete
//                        StemmerSpec provenance, span-aligned with tokens.
//    opennlp:expansions  positional, lexical-expansion values: relation, depth,
//                        sense rank, weight, and lexicon provenance per term.
//    opennlp:geo         positional, geo values: the geocoded resolution of each
//                        resolvable location entity, anchored on the mention's span
//                        (from PIPELINE_STEP_GEOCODE).
//    opennlp:normalization  document-scoped normalization values with alignment.
//    opennlp:analytics   document-scoped typed DocumentAnalytics values.
//    opennlp:chunk-groups  document-scoped strategy chunks, vectors, centroids,
//                        routes, and statistics.
//    opennlp:term-vectors document-scoped distinct terms, frequencies, occurrence
//                        spans, and source-layer provenance.
//    opennlp:dependencies positional dependency arcs, one per token, referencing
//                        head and dependent tokens by document token-layer index.
//    opennlp:relations   positional relations between named entities, referencing
//                        subject and object by document entity-layer index.

